---
description: Safety, git, production, database and performance guardrails for IndusCost.
alwaysApply: true
---

PROJECT: INDUSCOST

GENERAL
- This is a production business system.
- Preserve existing business semantics unless explicitly authorized.
- Prefer evidence from the repository over assumptions.
- Inspect existing architecture before creating new abstractions.
- Do not duplicate existing domain models, services, repositories or ledgers.
- Keep changes narrowly scoped to the requested mission.

GIT
- Never work directly on main for implementation missions.
- Before changing files, inspect branch, HEAD and git status.
- Use a clean dedicated branch/worktree.
- Never mix unrelated changes.
- Never reset or revert unrelated work.
- Report initial SHA and final SHA.

PRODUCTION SAFETY
- Never deploy unless explicitly requested.
- Never execute production migrations.
- Never modify production databases.
- Never alter cron, systemd, firewall, Cloudflare, Tailscale or AWS infrastructure unless explicitly requested.
- Never use production as a test database.
- Never expose credentials or .env contents.

DATABASE
- PostgreSQL is authoritative for application persistence.
- Prisma schema and migrations must be reviewed before database changes.
- No destructive migration without explicit authorization.
- Performance changes must be supported by measurements.
- Do not create indexes based solely on intuition; use query evidence and EXPLAIN when appropriate.

PERFORMANCE WORK
- Measure before optimizing.
- Separate frontend, network/API, backend processing and database time.
- Identify query counts, N+1 patterns, repeated work, payload size and expensive transformations.
- Use repeatable benchmarks with warm-up and multiple iterations.
- Do not claim improvement from a single run.
- Preserve financial results exactly.
- Profiling must be disabled by default and have negligible overhead when disabled.
- Do not log sensitive financial/customer data.

CASH FLOW
- Cash Flow/Treasury financial semantics must not change during performance work.
- Nomus remains the authoritative source for official AR/AP data according to existing architecture.
- Do not double-count PV, NF, DS and CR.
- Existing PERF 2C behavior must be preserved unless measurements demonstrate a concrete regression.

QUALITY
- Run relevant tests after modifications.
- Run build before declaring completion.
- Distinguish new errors from repository baseline errors.
- Do not fix unrelated technical debt.

REPORTING
- Be concise.
- Do not narrate every file read or tool call.
- Do not return huge discovery reports.
- Report evidence, measured bottlenecks, files changed, tests, build, SHA and real remaining risks.
